.TH QUERENCIA-ANMELDUNG 8 "2026-10-20" "querencia-anmeldung 0.1.1" "Querencia Desktop"
.SH NAME
querencia-anmeldung \- login screen of Querencia Desktop (greetd with ReGreet)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B querencia-anmeldung
.RI [ greetd-options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B querencia-anmeldung
runs
.BR greetd (1)
with the configuration
.IR /etc/querencia/greetd/config.toml .
greetd shows the graphical greeter ReGreet as user
.B _greetd
in a
.BR labwc (1)
compositor without menu or key bindings. By default it offers only the
Querencia Desktop sessions; see
.BR SESSIONS .
.PP
It is not meant to be run by hand; the service
.B querencia-anmeldung.service
starts it when it is the default display manager
.RI ( display-manager.service ).
.SH SESSIONS
Each time the login screen appears,
.I /usr/libexec/querencia-anmeldung/sitzungen-auswahl
builds the session list in
.I /run/querencia-anmeldung/wayland-sessions
from
.I /usr/local/share/wayland-sessions
and
.IR /usr/share/wayland-sessions .
It offers the sessions whose
.B DesktopNames
contain
.B X-Querencia
and other sessions only when they are enabled with
.B freigeben
in
.IR /etc/querencia/greetd/sitzungen.conf .
The bare labwc session, hidden sessions, broken session files and X11
sessions are never offered. Users without a valid last session get
\(lqQuerencia Desktop\(rq preselected.
.PP
Every offered session starts through
.IR /usr/libexec/querencia-anmeldung/sitzung-starten ,
which sets
.BR XDG_CURRENT_DESKTOP " (from " DesktopNames ),
.BR XDG_SESSION_DESKTOP " and " DESKTOP_SESSION
(from the file name) and
.B XDG_SESSION_TYPE=wayland
like GDM, then reads
.I /etc/profile
and
.I ~/.profile
and runs
.BR Exec .
.B huelle = nein
in
.I sitzungen.conf
starts the sessions without these variables (behaviour of 0.1.0).
.PP
GNOME needs GDM for its screen lock: under this login screen GNOME runs
without screen locking, even with the variables set. While GNOME is
installed, GDM stays the default display manager; enable GNOME in
.I sitzungen.conf
only on purpose.
.SH DEFAULT DISPLAY MANAGER
As with gdm3 and lightdm, the default display manager is recorded in
.I /etc/X11/default-display-manager
and in the debconf question
.BR shared/default-x-display-manager .
On installation the Querencia login screen becomes the default only when no
other display manager is set up, when it is chosen in that question, or when
.B QUERENCIA_ANMELDUNG=ja
is set. A running display manager is never stopped; a change takes effect
at the next boot.
.TP
.B sudo dpkg-reconfigure querencia-anmeldung
asks for the default display manager (for example gdm3 or
querencia-anmeldung).
.TP
.B sudo QUERENCIA_ANMELDUNG=nein dpkg-reconfigure querencia-anmeldung
switches back, without a question, to the display manager that was active
before (or to another installed one).
.PP
Removing the package restores the previous display manager, for example
GDM.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/querencia/greetd/config.toml
greetd configuration (virtual terminal 7, user _greetd).
.TP
.I /etc/querencia/greetd/regreet.toml
greeting, background, theme, clock.
.TP
.I /etc/querencia/greetd/sitzungen.conf
sessions offered next to Querencia Desktop, session wrapper on or off.
.TP
.I /etc/querencia/greetd/labwc/
labwc configuration of the login screen.
.TP
.I /var/log/querencia-anmeldung/log
ReGreet log.
.TP
.I /var/lib/querencia-anmeldung/
last chosen user and session.
.TP
.I /run/querencia-anmeldung/
session list for ReGreet and
.I auswahl.txt
(why each session file is offered or hidden).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR greetd (1),
.BR greetd (5),
.BR labwc (1),
.BR dpkg-reconfigure (8)
